{"conversation_id":"5ce419d6-b412-4191-998c-211974ffb6f6","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\"agent\":\"Frontend Engineer\",\"areas_affected\":[\"app/status/page.tsx\",\"components/status/StatusDashboard.tsx\",\"components/status/StatusCard.tsx\",\"components/status/StatusBadge.tsx\",\"components/layout/Footer.tsx\",\"types/index.ts\",\"tests/status.test.tsx\",\"app/api/status/route.ts\",\"docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md\"],\"contracts\":[\"GET /api/status -\\u003e 200 OK | 503 Service Unavailable: JSON payload with { status: 'healthy' | 'degraded' | 'unhealthy', version: string, environment: 'production' | 'staging' | 'development', timestamp: string, services?: { api: { status: 'up' | 'down', latency_ms?: number } } }\",\"Client Cache Contract: Client requests to /api/status must use cache: 'no-store' to ensure real-time status reporting without Next.js or browser stale caching.\",\"Frontend Error Boundary Contract: The frontend status page must render a graceful degraded/offline UI with retry capability if /api/status fails or returns non-200, rather than throwing an unhandled runtime error.\"],\"proposed_tasks\":[{\"depends_on\":[],\"description\":\"Implement backend health check endpoint GET /api/status returning API availability, backend version, application environment, timestamp, and optional service health metrics.\",\"id\":\"task-backend-status-api\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Backend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-backend-status-api\"],\"description\":\"Define TypeScript interfaces for status response in types/index.ts and implement client-side fetcher utility with error handling and no-cache configuration.\",\"id\":\"task-frontend-status-types-and-client\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-frontend-status-types-and-client\"],\"description\":\"Create modular status UI components (StatusDashboard, StatusCard, StatusBadge) displaying overall system health, API availability, backend version, environment indicator, and manual refresh button with accessible ARIA live states.\",\"id\":\"task-frontend-status-components\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-frontend-status-components\"],\"description\":\"Assemble the user-facing status page route at app/status/page.tsx and add discovery navigation link to the status page in components/layout/Footer.tsx.\",\"id\":\"task-frontend-status-page-route\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-frontend-status-page-route\"],\"description\":\"Implement unit and integration tests using Vitest and React Testing Library in tests/status.test.tsx covering loading states, successful status rendering, API degradation/failure fallbacks, and manual refresh interaction.\",\"id\":\"task-frontend-tests\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"},{\"depends_on\":[\"task-frontend-status-page-route\"],\"description\":\"Document the status page route, API contract, and usage in docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md and engineering guides.\",\"id\":\"task-documentation\",\"suggested_owner\":\"Frontend Engineer\"}],\"questions_or_unknowns\":[\"Should the status page be fully public or restricted to authenticated users/administrators?\",\"Is auto-polling (e.g. interval every 30s) required, or should refreshing be on-demand / manual only?\",\"Should backend version reflect the package.json version, a git commit SHA, or a deployment environment variable?\",\"Are sub-service statuses (e.g. Supabase database connectivity, external auth) expected in this phase or strictly top-level API availability?\"],\"risks\":[\"API downtime preventing status page rendering: If the status page crashes when the API is down, users cannot observe outage status; mitigated by client-side resilient error handling and graceful offline state.\",\"Stale status data due to aggressive caching: Next.js App Router or intermediate proxies caching the GET /api/status response; mitigated by setting Cache-Control: no-store on the endpoint and cache: 'no-store' in client fetch.\",\"Information disclosure: Leaking sensitive internal system paths or environment configuration in backend version or environment fields; mitigated by sanitizing backend status payload.\",\"Client refresh rate limit exhaustion: Rapid user or automated polling overwhelming the server; mitigated by debouncing manual refresh and limiting polling intervals.\"],\"summary\":\"Plan for implementing a user-facing health and status dashboard (/status) in Next.js 16 App Router. The frontend consumes a backend /api/status endpoint to display real-time API availability, backend version, application environment, and service latency. Includes client-side fetching with resilient fallback/error states, accessible UI status badges and cards with Tailwind CSS, auto/manual refresh controls, footer navigation integration, and Vitest component test suites.\",\"tests\":[\"Unit tests for StatusBadge and StatusCard rendering correct variant colors, icons, and labels across healthy, degraded, and down states.\",\"Integration test verifying loading skeleton displays while fetching status data.\",\"Integration test verifying accurate display of backend version, application environment, and API availability upon successful API response.\",\"Resilience test verifying fallback error UI ('API Unreachable' / 'Offline') when the endpoint returns 500 or network fails.\",\"Interaction test verifying manual refresh button re-triggers data fetch and updates the last-checked timestamp.\",\"Accessibility tests validating ARIA status role (role='status') and screen reader announcement tags.\"],\"toolAction\":\"Submitting status page plan\",\"toolSummary\":\"Submit status page plan\"}\n","duration_seconds":152.2126244,"num_turns":1,"structured_output":{"agent":"Frontend Engineer","areas_affected":["app/status/page.tsx","components/status/StatusDashboard.tsx","components/status/StatusCard.tsx","components/status/StatusBadge.tsx","components/layout/Footer.tsx","types/index.ts","tests/status.te